+ The Latvian Environment, Geology and Meteorology centre has developed the meteo.lv application. The application provides up-to-date hydrometeorological observations and forecast data, as well as warning data.The application uses the following data from data.gov.lv:
https://data.gov.lv/dati/lv/dataset/hidrometeorologiskie-noverojumi/resource/17460efb-ae99-4d1d-8144-1068f184b05f
https://data.gov.lv/dati/lv/dataset/hidrometeorologiskie-bridinajumi
https://data.gov.lv/dati/lv/dataset/meteorologiskas-prognozes-apdzivotam-vietam

The links below contain research and publications from over the years in the field of environmental protection and policy, including pollution, water quality and air:
https://ppdb.mk.gov.lv/petijuma_politikas_joma/vides-aizsardziba/?sf_paged=2;
https://ppdb.mk.gov.lv/petijuma_politikas_joma/vides-politika/;
https://ppdb.mk.gov.lv/petijuma_politikas_joma/vides-politika/?_sf_s=Gaisa%20kvalit%C4%81te
+ Every year, colleagues from the State Plant Protection Service carry out soil monitoring for agrochemical research on agricultural land. The monitoring has been carried out since 2009 and the data is available on the portal. It should be noted that the aim of the monitoring is to obtain information on the agrochemical performance of a representative sample of farms within the national planning regions, taking into account the farming system and farm specialisation. 
Links: https://www.vaad.gov.lv/lv/augsnes-monitoringa-rezultati;
https://data.gov.lv/dati/lv/dataset/augsnu-agrokimiskas-izpetes-rezultati

